        "# cFish.io WordPress Backup & Recovery Plan\r",
        "\r",
        "This document outlines the procedures for backing up the cFish.io WordPress website and recovering from potential disasters.\r",
        "\r",
        "## Backup Strategy\r",
        "\r",
        "### Regular Backup Schedule\r",
        "\r",
        "| Type | Frequency | Retention | Storage Location |\r",
        "|------|-----------|-----------|------------------|\r",
        "| Full Site | Weekly | 1 month | WordPress.com Jetpack Backups |\r",
        "| Database | Daily | 2 weeks | WordPress.com Jetpack Backups |\r",
        "| Manual | Before major changes | 3 months | Local Storage + External Drive |\r",
        "| Code Repository | Continuous | Indefinite | GitHub |\r",
        "\r",
        "### What to Back Up\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **WordPress Database**\r",
        "   - All content (posts, pages, comments)\r",
        "   - WordPress settings\r",
        "   - User accounts\r",
        "   - Plugin/theme settings\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **WordPress Files**\r",
        "   - Theme files (including customizations)\r",
        "   - Plugin files\r",
        "   - Uploads directory (images, media)\r",
        "   - Custom code\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Configuration Files**\r",
        "   - wp-config.php (sensitive - store securely)\r",
        "   - .htaccess files\r",
        "   - robots.txt\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Development Environment**\r",
        "   - Local database\r",
        "   - Local files\r",
        "   - Environment configuration\r",
        "\r",
        "## Backup Tools & Methods\r",
        "\r",
        "### WordPress.com/Jetpack Backups\r",
        "- Primary backup method\r",
        "- Automatic daily and weekly backups\r",
        "- One-click restore functionality\r",
        "- Verify backups monthly for integrity\r",
        "\r",
        "### Manual Backups\r",
        "- Perform before major site changes\r",
        "- Generate database SQL export\r",
        "- Export WordPress XML content\r",
        "- Download wp-content directory\r",
        "- Store in multiple locations\r",
        "\r",
        "### Code Repository Backup\r",
        "- All custom code in GitHub\r",
        "- Regular commits to development branch\r",
        "- Stable releases merged to main branch\r",
        "- Repositories configured with appropriate .gitignore\r",
        "\r",
        "## Disaster Recovery Procedures\r",
        "\r",
        "### Site Compromise (Hacking/Malware)\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Immediate Actions**\r",
        "   - Take site offline if necessary\r",
        "   - Change all passwords (WordPress, hosting, FTP)\r",
        "   - Document what happened\r",
        "   - Notify required stakeholders\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Assessment**\r",
        "   - Identify compromised files/database entries\r",
        "   - Check access logs for unauthorized entries\r",
        "   - Determine extent of the breach\r",
        "   - Evaluate most recent clean backup\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Recovery**\r",
        "   - Restore from most recent clean backup\r",
        "   - Scan restored files for remaining issues\r",
        "   - Update all software (WordPress, plugins, themes)\r",
        "   - Check file permissions\r",
        "   - Implement additional security measures\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Post-Recovery**\r",
        "   - Change all passwords again\r",
        "   - Document incident and response\r",
        "   - Review and improve security measures\r",
        "   - Perform full security audit\r",
        "\r",
        "### Data Loss/Corruption\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Immediate Actions**\r",
        "   - Assess extent of data loss\r",
        "   - Document what data was affected\r",
        "   - Determine cause (user error, system failure, etc.)\r",
        "   - Take site offline if necessary\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Recovery Options**\r",
        "   - Restore from WordPress.com/Jetpack backup\r",
        "   - Restore from manual backup if needed\r",
        "   - Restore code from GitHub repository\r",
        "   - Recreate any lost configuration\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Verification**\r",
        "   - Test site functionality\r",
        "   - Verify data integrity\r",
        "   - Check for missing content or customizations\r",
        "   - Restore any missing elements manually\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Post-Recovery**\r",
        "   - Document incident and response\r",
        "   - Improve backup procedures if needed\r",
        "   - Address root cause of data loss\r",
        "\r",
        "### Server/Hosting Failure\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Immediate Actions**\r",
        "   - Contact WordPress.com support\r",
        "   - Document issue and response\r",
        "   - Assess expected downtime\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Temporary Measures**\r",
        "   - Consider emergency temporary site if needed\r",
        "   - Communicate status to users via alternate channels\r",
        "\r",
        "3. **Recovery**\r",
        "   - Work with WordPress.com to restore service\r",
        "   - Verify site functionality after restoration\r",
        "   - Restore from backups if necessary\r",
        "\r",
        "4. **Post-Recovery**\r",
        "   - Document incident and response\r",
        "   - Evaluate hosting provider reliability\r",
        "   - Consider redundancy options if needed\r",
        "\r",
        "## Local Development Recovery\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Loss of Local Environment**\r",
        "   - Clone repository from GitHub\r",
        "   - Create fresh local WordPress installation\r",
        "   - Import database from production or backup\r",
        "   - Configure wp-config.php for local environment\r",
        "   - Update site URLs in database\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Synchronization After Recovery**\r",
        "   - Pull latest code from GitHub\r",
        "   - Export fresh database from production\r",
        "   - Import production database to local environment\r",
        "   - Update site URLs for local development\r",
        "\r",
        "## Testing Recovery Procedures\r",
        "\r",
        "To ensure recovery procedures work when needed:\r",
        "\r",
        "1. **Quarterly Testing**\r",
        "   - Test database restore process\r",
        "   - Verify file restoration\r",
        "   - Practice local environment recreation\r",
        "   - Document any issues and improve procedures\r",
        "\r",
        "2. **Annual Full Recovery Test**\r",
        "   - Simulate full disaster recovery\r",
        "   - Create test environment from backups\r",
        "   - Verify full functionality\r",
        "   - Document recovery time and any issues\r",
        "\r",
        "## Password Recovery & Access Management\r",
        "\r",
        "### Recovery Access Documentation\r",
        "\r",
        "Maintain secure documentation of:\r",
        "- Admin account recovery procedures\r",
        "- Database access credentials\r",
        "- WordPress.com account recovery options\r",
        "- GitHub access recovery\r",
        "- Hosting control panel access\r",
        "\r",
        "### Access Redundancy\r",
        "\r",
        "- Multiple admin users with appropriate permissions\r",
        "- Multiple team members with GitHub access\r",
        "- Documented procedures for credential recovery\r",
        "- Secure sharing of recovery information\r",
        "\r",
        "## Recovery Documentation\r",
        "\r",
        "After any recovery operation, document:\r",
        "1. Incident details (what happened, when, impact)\r",
        "2. Recovery steps taken\r",
        "3. Time to recovery\r",
        "4. Any data or functionality loss\r",
        "5. Lessons learned\r",
        "6. Improvements to implement\r",
        "\r",
        "## Appendices\r",
        "\r",
        "### A. Backup Verification Checklist\r",
        "\r",
        "- [ ] Database backup contains all tables\r",
        "- [ ] File backup includes all themes\r",
        "- [ ] File backup includes all plugins\r",
        "- [ ] File backup includes all uploads\r",
        "- [ ] Custom code backed up to GitHub\r",
        "- [ ] Backup storage verified and secure\r",
        "\r",
        "### B. Emergency Contact Information\r",
        "\r",
        "- WordPress.com Support: https://wordpress.com/support/\r",
        "- Domain Registrar: [Your Registrar Info]\r",
        "- Team Emergency Contacts: [Team Member List]\r",
